The B2B Marketing Pipeline Impact Measurement Framework and Insights Dashboard was developed to establish a single source of truth for measuring how marketing activities translate into pipeline and revenue outcomes. Prior to this initiative, marketing-generated and marketing-influenced opportunities were fragmented across systems and calculated manually, limiting visibility into true marketing contribution and reducing confidence in investment decisions.

To address this, we designed a robust framework that classifies opportunities as Marketing Generated (MG), Marketing Influenced (MI), or Not Influenced using standardized business logic. Leveraging this framework, we launched an enterprise-wide Tableau Insights Dashboard that provides end-to-end visibility across businesses, regions, channels, and funnel stages. The solution enables leadership to evaluate marketing effectiveness through pipeline, win rate, deal size, and velocity metrics, significantly strengthening Sales and Marketing alignment.

The initiative has already delivered measurable business impact, including FY26 YTD pipeline contributions of $220M MG and $580M MI, with strong adoption across the organization with 159+ unique users and 4,100+ views. The dashboard received recognition from Frank Cooper, CMO of Visa and was highlighted in the FY26 Q2 recap for unlocking visibility into marketing-driven revenue potential. Additionally, the success and cross-functional impact of this framework contributed to securing a new client logo, KKR, resulting in a strategic $336K project opportunity for LatentView.





TECHNOLOGY AND INNOVATION - EVALUATION PARAMETERS:
• In-demand (Trending tech): Demonstrate working on cutting-edge technology and
how it effectively addresses a client pain point.
• Scale of Work (Scalability): Articulation of the magnitude of the innovation – in terms
of the downstream impact of the innovation in the client organization and its
processes.
• Idea: Demonstrating that the idea for the innovation was generated by the team and
not by the client. Co-creation can be considered as long as the team is able to
demonstrate their contribution to the idea and that it significantly enhances the idea.
• New product/Process transformation: Creating a completely new
product/process. This product could be client specific or can be cross pollinated, how
the team has evolved over the course of the engagement – it could be with respect to
skill development, project management practices, team health, client’s impression of
the team, etc.
• Unique Value Proposition: Articulation of how this innovation can help LatentView
communicate a stronger value proposition to its clients – the team can demonstrate
how this innovative idea can be implemented in other use cases or how this innovative
idea helped LatentView acquire a new logo or a new business within an existing logo.
